{
  "document_id": "e9ccf2482ca3b6c3cf6d7ea0c1315dbd",
  "markdown_content": "The amortization periods for the costs incurred to obtain a customer contract is determined at a portfolio level due to the similarities within these customer contract portfolios.\n\nOther costs, such as general costs or costs related to past performance obligations, are expensed as incurred.\n\nDeferred contract costs are classified as current or non-current within prepaid expenses ans   o s o t st - e rt  t osts as of December 31, 2019 and 2018, included in the balance sheet were as follows:\n\n|                            | 2019    | 2018    |\n|----------------------------|---------|---------|\n| Assets                     |         |         |\n| Prepaid expenses and other | $ 3,027 | $ 2,347 |\n| Other assets - net         | 1,824   | 1,831   |\n| Total                      | $ 4,851 | $ 4,178 |\n\nFor the years ended December 31, 2019 and 2018, the Partnership recognized wo    cs t t  w t sot deferred contract costs, primarily within selling, general and administrative expenses in the statements of income.\n\nDeferred contract costs are assessed for impairment on an annual basis. An impairment charge is recognized to the extent the carrying amount of a deferred cost exceeds the remaining amount of consideration expected to be received in exchange for the goods ar  r s r      s s ts ng tho   e       s   vve been no impairment charges recognized for the year ended December 31, 2019 and 2018.\n\n## 4. WIRELESS DEVICE PAYMENT PLANS\n\nUnder the Verizon Wireless device payment program, eligible customers can purchase wireless devices under a device payment plan agreement. Customers that activate service on devices purchased under the device payment program pay lower service fees as compared to those under fixed-term service plans, and their device payment plan charge is included on their wireless monthly bill. Verizon Wireless only offers fixedterm plans to business customers.",
